,"content_en\u002F1.getting-started\u002F4.installation\u002F4.kubernetes-helm.md","Kubernetes: Using Helm",{"type":204,"value":205,"toc":515},"minimark",[206,218,226,231,240,244,247,289,293,296,315,322,328,353,359,379,382,386,392,432,436,439,472,486,490,498,503,511],[207,208,209,210,217],"p",{},"For installation to Kubernetes, a Helm chart is available in our charts repository. The source code of the chart(s) is available on ",[211,212,216],"a",{"href":213,"rel":214},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Ffivenet-app\u002Fcharts",[215],"nofollow","GitHub fivenet-app\u002Fcharts",".",[207,219,220,221,225],{},"Before you begin, review the ",[211,222,224],{"href":223},"..\u002Frequirements","requirements"," and make sure your database, NATS server, storage, domain, and cluster ingress are ready.",[227,228,230],"h2",{"id":229},"_0-prerequisites","0. Prerequisites",[207,232,233,234,239],{},"This guide assumes you have a working Kubernetes cluster and a Helm client installed. If you haven't set up a Kubernetes cluster yet, please refer to the ",[211,235,238],{"href":236,"rel":237},"https:\u002F\u002Fkubernetes.io\u002Fdocs\u002Fsetup\u002F",[215],"Kubernetes installation guide",".\nYou can use any Kubernetes cluster, including local clusters like Minikube or KinD, or cloud providers like GKE, EKS, or AKS.",[227,241,243],{"id":242},"_1-add-helm-chart-repo","1. Add Helm Chart Repo",[207,245,246],{},"Add the FiveNet Helm chart repository to your Helm client:",[248,249,254],"pre",{"className":250,"code":251,"language":252,"meta":253,"style":253},"language-bash shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","helm repo add fivenet https:\u002F\u002Ffivenet.app\u002Fcharts\nhelm repo update\n","bash","",[255,256,257,279],"code",{"__ignoreMap":253},[258,259,262,266,270,273,276],"span",{"class":260,"line":261},"line",1,[258,263,265],{"class":264},"sBMFI","helm",[258,267,269],{"class":268},"sfazB"," repo",[258,271,272],{"class":268}," add",[258,274,275],{"class":268}," fivenet",[258,277,278],{"class":268}," https:\u002F\u002Ffivenet.app\u002Fcharts\n",[258,280,282,284,286],{"class":260,"line":281},2,[258,283,265],{"class":264},[258,285,269],{"class":268},[258,287,288],{"class":268}," update\n",[227,290,292],{"id":291},"_2-create-a-namespace","2. Create a Namespace",[207,294,295],{},"Create a dedicated namespace for FiveNet if you do not already have one:",[248,297,299],{"className":250,"code":298,"language":252,"meta":253,"style":253},"kubectl create namespace fivenet\n",[255,300,301],{"__ignoreMap":253},[258,302,303,306,309,312],{"class":260,"line":261},[258,304,305],{"class":264},"kubectl",[258,307,308],{"class":268}," create",[258,310,311],{"class":268}," namespace",[258,313,314],{"class":268}," fivenet\n",[227,316,318,319],{"id":317},"_3-get-the-latest-valuesyaml","3. Get the Latest ",[255,320,321],{},"values.yaml",[207,323,324,325,327],{},"Retrieve the default ",[255,326,321],{}," file for the Helm chart to start configuring your deployment:",[248,329,331],{"className":250,"code":330,"language":252,"meta":253,"style":253},"helm show values fivenet\u002Ffivenet > values.yaml\n",[255,332,333],{"__ignoreMap":253},[258,334,335,337,340,343,346,350],{"class":260,"line":261},[258,336,265],{"class":264},[258,338,339],{"class":268}," show",[258,341,342],{"class":268}," values",[258,344,345],{"class":268}," fivenet\u002Ffivenet",[258,347,349],{"class":348},"sMK4o"," >",[258,351,352],{"class":268}," values.yaml\n",[227,354,356,357],{"id":355},"_4-configure-valuesyaml","4. Configure ",[255,358,321],{},[207,360,361,362,364,365,369,370,373,374,378],{},"Edit the ",[255,363,321],{}," file to suit your deployment needs. Follow the ",[211,366,368],{"href":367},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Fconfiguration\u002Fconfigure","Configure FiveNet guide"," for the required settings in ",[255,371,372],{},".fivenet.config",", then use the ",[211,375,377],{"href":376},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Freference\u002Fconfig-reference","Config File Reference"," for individual options.",[207,380,381],{},"At a minimum, you should review the FiveNet configuration, secrets, persistence, and how the deployment should be exposed in your cluster.",[227,383,385],{"id":384},"_5-install-or-upgrade-fivenet","5. Install or Upgrade FiveNet",[207,387,388,389,391],{},"Deploy or update FiveNet in your Kubernetes cluster using the configured ",[255,390,321],{}," file:",[248,393,395],{"className":250,"code":394,"language":252,"meta":253,"style":253},"helm upgrade --install fivenet fivenet\u002Ffivenet \\\n  --namespace fivenet \\\n  -f values.yaml\n",[255,396,397,415,424],{"__ignoreMap":253},[258,398,399,401,404,407,409,411],{"class":260,"line":261},[258,400,265],{"class":264},[258,402,403],{"class":268}," upgrade",[258,405,406],{"class":268}," --install",[258,408,275],{"class":268},[258,410,345],{"class":268},[258,412,414],{"class":413},"sTEyZ"," \\\n",[258,416,417,420,422],{"class":260,"line":281},[258,418,419],{"class":268},"  --namespace",[258,421,275],{"class":268},[258,423,414],{"class":413},[258,425,427,430],{"class":260,"line":426},3,[258,428,429],{"class":268},"  -f",[258,431,352],{"class":268},[227,433,435],{"id":434},"_6-verify-the-deployment","6. Verify the Deployment",[207,437,438],{},"After the Helm release is installed, verify that the workloads are starting correctly:",[248,440,442],{"className":250,"code":441,"language":252,"meta":253,"style":253},"kubectl get pods -n fivenet\nhelm status fivenet -n fivenet\n",[255,443,444,459],{"__ignoreMap":253},[258,445,446,448,451,454,457],{"class":260,"line":261},[258,447,305],{"class":264},[258,449,450],{"class":268}," get",[258,452,453],{"class":268}," pods",[258,455,456],{"class":268}," -n",[258,458,314],{"class":268},[258,460,461,463,466,468,470],{"class":260,"line":281},[258,462,265],{"class":264},[258,464,465],{"class":268}," status",[258,467,275],{"class":268},[258,469,456],{"class":268},[258,471,314],{"class":268},[207,473,474,475,477,478,481,482,485],{},"Ensure that FiveNet is externally reachable as configured in your ",[255,476,321],{}," file, for example through your configured ",[255,479,480],{},"Ingress",", ",[255,483,484],{},"Service",", hostnames, and TLS settings.",[227,487,489],{"id":488},"_7-post-installation-steps","7. Post-Installation Steps",[207,491,492,493,497],{},"After installation, follow the ",[211,494,496],{"href":495},"post-install-steps","post-installation steps"," to complete the setup.",[499,500,502],"h3",{"id":501},"troubleshooting","Troubleshooting",[207,504,505,506,510],{},"For common issues during Kubernetes or Helm installation, such as database-related errors, refer to the ",[211,507,509],{"href":508},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Ftroubleshooting\u002Finstallation-issues","Database and Installation Troubleshooting"," page.",[512,513,514],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sBMFI, html code.shiki .sBMFI{--shiki-light:#E2931D;--shiki-default:#FFCB6B;--shiki-dark:#FFCB6B}html pre.shiki code .sfazB, html code.shiki .sfazB{--shiki-light:#91B859;--shiki-default:#C3E88D;--shiki-dark:#C3E88D}html .light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html.light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .dark .shiki sp